From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:29:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] Test MVCC and shared-mode logs that cannot sync under
 the decisions

MvccUnsyncableLog_Tests and SharedUnsyncableLog_Tests keep their slot
reuse coverage (slots cleared without a durable sync are never reused,
readers keep their snapshot, crash images recover exactly) with
"durable commits=false" (default A). New durable cases assert that the
snapshot checkpoint whose log stops syncing while it clears slots throws,
records the failure, keeps reads exact and refuses later writes without
reusing a slot; in shared mode the connection keeps the failure, and a
second connection's proof refuses its first commit before it writes.
SharedDurability_Tests: a shared commit whose log stops syncing now fails
with an unknown outcome and the connection stays read-only until
reopened (decision 6, default C); opted-out commits are not failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
